each request with reqID (makeReqID/parseReqID, main.go:308-337) so receive goroutines can compute latency and feed the aggregator (latencyAggregator, main.go:40-66).\",\n        \"Server stats logger (server.go:328-395) emits per-worker and aggregate lines that scripts/monitoring can scrape.\"\n      ],\n      \"downstream\": [\n        \"Server relies on internal/server/ebpf.go + generated internal/ebpfutil bindings.\",\n        \"Client output is parsed by run.sh’s Python aggregator; logs feed human debugging.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"name\": \"Support scripts\",\n      \"artefacts\": [\n        \"scripts/build_ebpf.sh:1-34\",\n        \"scripts/cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh:1-25\",\n        \"scripts/launch_server.sh:1-96\",\n        \"scripts/dispatch_docker_experiments.py:1-654\",\n        \"workload/run_client.sh:1-62\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Reusable helpers for building eBPF assets, cleaning pinned maps, launching the server standalone, dispatching dockerized experiments, and invoking the workload client without run.sh.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"build_ebpf.sh enforces clang availability, sets BPF_CLANG/BPF_CFLAGS, adds arch include paths, then runs `go generate ./internal/ebpfutil`.\",\n        \"cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh deletes global pinned maps unless run-specific BPF_PIN_PATH is set, preventing fd leaks between runs.\",\n        \"launch_server.sh builds cmd/pebble_server (unless disabled), enforces single instance via PID file, applies taskset when SERVER_CPUSET is exported, and records PID for run.sh.\",\n        \"dispatch_docker_experiments.py reads NUMA topology (read_numa_cpu_map, line 106), assigns per-container CPU slices, constructs docker run commands (build_jobs, line 149), streams logs asynchronously (run_job, line 221), and optionally post-processes with run_exp.py.\",\n        \"workload/run_client.sh is a thin CLI around `go run ./cmd/workload_client` for ad-hoc manual traffic.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"modules\": {\n    \"run_exp.py\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Top-level wrapper to sweep policies/rates and collect workload_summary.json files into one experiment summary.\",\n      \"key_points\": [\n        \"parse_args exposes knobs for policies/rates, send-workers, duration, server/client cores, plotting, and manifest reuse.\",\n        \"invoke_run_sh executes run.sh and captures the run directory; load_manifest_runs + link_run_directories reuse docker-dispatched runs.\",\n        \"generate_overall_plot / generate_get_scan_plot optionally render PNGs (skip with --skip-plot).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"run.sh\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Automation glue that sets up CPU pinning, rebuilds eBPF assets, runs cmd/pebble_server + cmd/workload_client for N iterations, and emits workload_summary.json.\",\n      \"key_points\": [\n        \"resolve_cpu_pool + join_by compute SERVER_CPUSET/CLIENT_CPUSET and export them for both taskset prefixes.\",\n        \"start_server/stop_server wrap scripts/launch_server.sh and enforce clean PID files; run_client pins workload_client under CLIENT_CPUSET.\",\n        \"Embedded Python generates workload_summary.json from logs/workload_iteration_*.txt, which run_exp.py later ingests.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"cmd/pebble_server\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Go binary that instantiates internal/server.Server based on CLI flags and keeps it running with profiling enabled.\",\n      \"key_sections\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Flag wiring & filesystem setup\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:21-52\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Defines flags for listen addr, workers, policy, max scan, log/results dirs, timeouts, and synthetic delays; ensures directories exist before logging.\",\n            \"Creates/opens <log-dir>/server.log (append mode) and builds a microsecond-resolution logger.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Profiling + server lifecycle\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:52-92\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Enables block/mutex profiling (runtime.SetBlockProfileRate/SetMutexProfileFraction) and hosts net/http/pprof on 127.0.0.1:6060.\",\n            \"Builds server.Config, calls server.New (fails fast on invalid config or eBPF load issues), installs SIGINT/SIGTERM handler, logs startup configuration, and blocks on srv.Run(ctx).\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"Uses internal/server (Config, Server, eBPF loader).\",\n        \"scripts/launch_server.sh expects -log-dir and -results-dir to exist for log collation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"cmd/workload_client\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Open-loop UDP workload generator with reqID-based latency measurement and throughput reporting.\",\n      \"key_sections\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Latency data structures\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:32-66\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"latencyRecord and latencyAggregator store per-request latencies, split into overall/GET/SCAN slices; aggregator.totalRecv reports sample counts.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Main workload loop\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:67-307\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Parses flags (server, duration, rate, get-frac, scan-limit, key prefix/space, log path, send workers), validates arguments, seeds RNGs per worker.\",\n            \"Creates a shared rate limiter (golang.org/x/time/rate), spawns send goroutines that build payloads (buildPayload, line 363) and assign reqIDs (makeReqID, line 308).\",\n            \"Spawns recv goroutines with deadlines that parse responses, extract reqIDs (parseReqID, line 320), compute latency, and push records into latencyCh.\",\n            \"Aggregator + monitor goroutines track outstanding requests and total received counts.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Statistics reporting\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:308-451\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Helper functions (makeReqID/parseReqID/writeHex/parseHex) ensure both sides share the encoding.\",\n            \"percentile/average/reportLatencyStats (lines 376-451) sort copies of the latency slices, compute p50/p90/p99/avg, and print textual summaries that run.sh’s regex parser expects.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"run.sh’s run_client wrapper invokes this with -log pointing at logs/client.log; workload/run_client.sh uses go run for convenience.\",\n        \"Server assumes GET payload format 'GET key [reqID]' and SCAN 'SCAN start limit [reqID]' as implemented here.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"internal/server\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Core server runtime, including configuration validation, UDP worker pool, request parser, stats logging, and eBPF policy integration.\",\n      \"key_files\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/config.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Config struct + Validate clamp runtime knobs to sane defaults so CLI/script errors don’t crash the server.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Config.Validate\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/config.go:19-43\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Sets ListenAddr default (127.0.0.1:9000), ensures at least one worker, caps MaxScanKeys >= 1 (default 100k), enforces non-zero timeouts/delays.\",\n                \"Called by server.New before any socket/eBPF work, giving run.sh freedom to pass zero/negative placeholder values.\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/server.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Implements the Server struct, worker lifecycle, UDP handler, and stats reporter.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Server.New\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:104-131\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Validates config, builds default logger when nil, loads eBPF policy via loadEBPF, clears pinned target map when a program is present, and preallocates workerStats.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Server.Run\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:144-182\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Resets stats, spawns stats logger, iterates workers to open UDP sockets (openWorker, lines 184-230), optionally attaches the eBPF program to worker 0, records socket fds into the pinned map, launches spawnWorker goroutines, and blocks until ctx cancellation.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"openWorker + spawnWorker\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:184-266\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"openWorker sets SO_REUSEADDR/SO_REUSEPORT via net.ListenConfig.Control and attaches the eBPF program once; returns both UDPConn and fd for map updates.\",\n                \"spawnWorker loops on ReadFromUDP, handles ctx cancellation/ErrClosed gracefully, and logs transient read/write errors.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"handleRequest\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:268-325\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Parses payloads via parseRequest, extracts optional reqID tokens, enforces SCAN limit <= MaxScanKeys, executes accurate busy-wait delays for GET/SCAN, records latencies per worker, and formats responses (formatResponse, lines 397-407).\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"startStatsLogger\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:328-395\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Every second, snapshots worker metrics, logs per-worker averages when